# L §5.18 example ask q9, copied, over a minimal reality: konto opens at 1 000.00 PLN on 2026-07-01; rent of 800.00
# PLN leaves on each month's first day, a pay of 700.00 PLN arrives in the window of the 15th to the 20th.
# "low(x, a .. b) from t: the lowest end-of-day balance of x on days a..b: min(bal(x, d) from t ...)" (L §5.14.1);
# the projection "starts from x's balance at the start of day t, and counts every movement dated on t through d";
# `windows each` on the projection read (L §4.4 "for that read"): wherever in its window each pay lands, it lands
# after the month's 1st.  Balances after each
# 1st: 200, 100 (the pay adds 700 back): low = 100.00 PLN on 2026-08-01 whatever the pays' days, so one plain line
# (writer 8: windows latest is gone; the run is 2026-07-01..2026-08-31, so windows each meets two windows).  Without a windows
# clause the projection meets a window: HOLE-IMPRECISE (L §5.14.1, §8.1).
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-07-01
  start 2026-07-01
  end 2026-08-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

kind accounts_pl: place PLN signed
place landlord: outside lives 1900-01-01..
place employer: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input rent_amt: money PLN
input pay_amt: money PLN
input w_lo: int
input w_hi: int

move rent[m in months]: transfers
  on start_of(m)
  leg cash from konto to landlord amount rent_amt

move pay[m in months]: transfers
  on window(add_days(start_of(m), w_lo), add_days(start_of(m), w_hi))
  leg cash from employer to konto amount pay_amt

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2025-12-01
  accounts_pl + [konto] lives 2019-05-01..
  rent_amt = 800.00 PLN
  pay_amt = 700.00 PLN
  w_lo = 14
  w_hi = 19
  opening[konto] = 1 000.00 PLN at 2026-07-01 start

ask q9: low(konto, 2026-07-01 .. 2026-08-31) from 2026-07-01 windows each law 2026-07-01
ask q9b: low(konto, 2026-07-01 .. 2026-08-31) from 2026-07-01 law 2026-07-01
=== expect
q9: 100.00 PLN
  law date 2026-07-01, cut 2026-07-01
q9b: ?"date within window(2026-07-15, 2026-07-20) not precise enough for ...
  law date 2026-07-01, cut 2026-07-01
